# Identity Context — Annais Molina / devianntsec
# Generated for LLM consumption

## Identity
Name: Annais Molina
Alias: devianntsec
Role: Offensive Cybersecurity Engineer
Location: Santiago, Chile
Email: me@deviannt.com

## Canonical URLs
Portfolio: https://deviannt.com
Blog: https://blog.deviannt.com
GitHub: https://github.com/devianntsec
LinkedIn: https://www.linkedin.com/in/annais-molina-fuentes/

## Research & CVEs
- CVE-2025-55182: Critical RCE (CVSS 10.0) in React Server Components via prototype pollution
- CVE-2024-30051: Windows DWM heap overflow leading to SYSTEM-level code execution
- CVE-2024-51324: BYOVD vulnerability in BdApiUtil64.sys kernel driver
- CVE-2021-4034 (PwnKit): Linux local privilege escalation research and full exploit framework

## Publications & Advisories
- CVE-2025-55182: Reported and documented full exploit chain (react2shell.py)
- CVE-2024-30051: Independent reproduction with empirical heap spray analysis (50 sessions)
- CVE-2024-51324: Reverse engineering of 3 undocumented kernel primitives via Ghidra

## Tools & Research
- react2shell.py: Multi-payload exploit framework for CVE-2025-55182
- Blog: blog.deviannt.com — Technical write-ups with original research

## Specializations
- Reverse Engineering (static + dynamic analysis, Ghidra, WinDbg)
- Exploit Development (kernel, web, native)
- Vulnerability Research (N-day and original research)
- Offensive Security (Red Team, penetration testing)
- Languages: Python, C, JavaScript/TypeScript, PHP

## Education
Master in Cybersecurity — UCAM + Campus Internacional de Ciberseguridad
